menu "Station: availability ledger"

    config LEDGER_TARGET_PERMILLE
        int "Daily availability target (per mille)"
        range 900 1000
        default 980
        help
            Onocoy's daily availability target. 980 = 98.0 %, which allows
            about 28.8 minutes of downtime per UTC day. Planned downtime
            (receiver flashing) is only scheduled within what is left.

    config LEDGER_HISTORY_DAYS
        int "Days of per-day history kept"
        range 7 90
        default 30

    config LEDGER_ALIVE_PERSIST_S
        int "Persist the last-alive mark every (s)"
        range 10 600
        default 60
        help
            After a power cut, the time between this mark and the next boot
            is counted as downtime. Shorter is more exact but writes NVS
            more often (60 s is about 1500 page erases per page in 10 years
            with the 112 KB NVS partition).

endmenu
